+## Hostile pets, emergency escape and duel isolation
+
+- Put a hunter or warlock pet on a mage while its owner is Polymorphed. The
+  mage must attempt species-valid control first, damage the pet when control is
+  unavailable, and continue using the sheep window for movement or recovery.
+- Move either a hostile player or its pet inside eight yards of a mage. Blink
+  must face away from the closest active pressure source; Frost Nova/Cone of
+  Cold are the fallback. Repeat for a hunter at ten yards and verify Disengage,
+  Freezing Trap/Wing Clip, then continued retreat to preferred range.
+- Bring an active pet below 30% health, or below 65% while its owner is under
+  protected control. The duel target planner must keep the pet selected until
+  the kill response completes, without breaking control on the owner.
+- Apply breakable control to the pet itself. The bot must not damage it merely
+  because the owner is also controlled.
+- Add a priest, paladin or other support bot to the duelist's group. During
+  countdown and active duel it must not dispel, heal or buff either participant;
+  the two participants' self-casts and hostile casts remain allowed.
